p.seg:
; a favourite eristic formula: see Ar. Clouds 1174
								τοῦτο τοὐπιχώριον | ἀτεχνῶς
							ἐπανθεῖ, τὸ τί λέγεις σύ;

div.p:
ff. The phase of Greek religious life here censured is illustrated by
						Dieterich Nek. pp. 81 f. and Rohde Psyche^{2}
						II 74 ff.: cf. also Lobeck Aglaoph. pp. 643 ff.

p.seg:
: sacrificial liturgies. A θυηπολικόν is mentioned by Suidas (s.v. Ὀρφεύς) as one of the ‘works’ of Orpheus:
							see also Lobeck Aglaoph. p. 371 and Rohde Psyche^{2}
							II pp. 112, 113 notes

 Aristotle disappointed Plato's
							expectations: for he will not admit that such arrangements are even ὠφέλιμα (Pol. B 1. 1261^{a}
							2 ff.).

: ‘prove themselves to be’ (J.
							and C.), rather than ‘grow to be’ (D. and V.): cf. III 412 C οἱ δὲ γεωργῶν ἄριστοι ἆρ’ οὐ γεωργικώτατοι
								γίγνονται;
